Release Notes unified i.MX6 Linux BSP:
======================================

BSP-Yocto-i.MX6-PD18.1.0                2018-08-06
==================================================
- Linux Kernel v4.14.39 (v4.14 is a LTS kernel)
  * Update from v4.1.46 to v4.14.39
- barebox v2017.12.0
- Yocto 2.4.3 (rocko)
- Qt 5.9.6 from meta-qt5 (rocko)

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- phytec-qt5demo-image

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 16.04 64Bit

Machines:
---------
- Added:
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-8
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-13
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-14
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-15
  * phyboard-nunki-imx6-1

- No longer supported:
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-6
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-7 (replaced by phyboard-mira-imx6-14, see Notes)
  * phyboard-subra-imx6-1
  * phyboard-subra-imx6-2
  * phycard-imx6-1


Changes since PD16.1.1:
-----------------------
- New Features:
  * barebox: USB host and OTG support
  * barebox: DFU file transfer is now supported
  * Etnaviv GPU driver
    - Replaced proprietary Vivante GPU driver
    - Qt5 support
    - OpenGL support
  * RAUC (Robust Auto-Update Controller)
    - Only supported with NAND flash (no eMMC support)
    - barebox scripts for partitioning and flashing of the NAND flash
    - RAUC update tool in userspace
    - Yocto support for building rauc bundles
    - Default enabled on Kits (phyboard-mira-imx6-3 and phyflex-imx6-2)
  * phyBOARD-Nunki Imaging baseboard support
  * Following phyCAM cameras are supported with this BSP:
    - VM-009
    - VM-010
    - VM-011
    - VM-012
    - VM-050 (thermal vision)
  * New phytec-vision-image for vision and imaging purposes:
    - Includes openCV library
  * Updated version of the bayer2rgb-neon library
  * New QtDemo version 1.3

- Fixes:
  * kernel:
    - Display and HDMI are now working with the i.MX 6QuadPlus.
    - Fixed UART RX Fifo Overrun issue


Known Issues:
-------------
- general:
  * Decoding H264 videos with the VPU in our Qt5 demo flickers and shows
    wrong artefacts. Outside of Qt decoding H264 videos works well.
  * The internal watchdog of the i.MX 6 cannot be used. We recommend to use
    the PMIC watchdog as preconfigured.

- barebox:
  * In rare cases (< 0.5%) during boot the ethernet phy does not come up
    correctly and Ethernet is not working
  * The first attempt to read a subdiretory structure over tftp might fail.
    Following attempts work.

- kernel:
  * In rare cases (< 0.1%) during kernel boot the NAND flash fails to be
    detected with following error:
    gpmi_reset_block(f0a2a000): module reset timeout.
  * 1.2 GHz i.MX 6:
    - Controlling ARM and SOC voltages for DVFS with PMIC is not supported
      since the 1.2 GHz operating point is not allowed to be operated with
      the internal i.MX 6 LDO's in bypass mode. So this machine always
      operates with internal LDO's enabled which results in highly more heat
      generation on the SOC.
    - Boot from eMMC on this SOM often leads to boot hangs specific to this
      1.2 GHz variant.
  * HDMI audio module driver is disabled due to imcompatibility issues with
    alsa.
  * The Microphone and Line-In inputs on the phyFLEX-i.MX6 do not work.
  * After resuming from suspend ethernet is not coming up correctly.
  * On SOMs with 1 GB RAM size a CMA size of 256 MB is not supported when
    the imx legacy framebuffer is used.
  * The LDB_DI0_SEL and LDB_DI1_SEL mux can only be set in the
    devicetree and cannot be changed on runtime.
  * RS485 half duplex operation is broken.


Notes:
------
- The phyboard-mira-imx6-7 machines represented a phyCORE-i.MX 6DualLight SOM
  with 1 GB RAM and eMMC on a phyBOARD-Mira low-cost. With this release it
  got replaced by the phyboard-mira-imx6-14 which represents the same SOM but
  on a phyBOARD-Mira full-featured so that the SOM now supports all the
  features of the full-featured phyBOARD-Mira.
